course: dictionary
lesson: 3655
title: Firstborn and family words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Firstborn is made of two smaller words: first and born. Put them together and you get the first child born to a family, the eldest child. When you meet a new word, look inside it for clues you already know.
explain: «Ten plagues struck Egypt, from the river Nile turning to blood to the death of the firstborn.» The sentence is about a family and about a serious, important event. Ask what word would fit: the first child born to a family makes sense, so firstborn means exactly that.
explain: Firstborn can be a noun, as in «her firstborn», or an adjective, as in «firstborn son». The noun has a plural too: firstborns. Watch the word around it to tell which kind you are reading.
fact: Firstborn means the first child born to a family; another word for it is eldest child.
fact: Firstborn is made from two words: first and born.
fact: In the Bible, the firstborn son had special rights and duties.
fact: A good check is to swap in eldest child and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: Which word fits the gap? «Ana's ___ son is three, and her second son is one.» | Middle | Twin | *Firstborn | Youngest
exercise: «Ten plagues struck Egypt, from the river Nile turning to blood to the death of the firstborn.» What is the firstborn in this sentence? | The river Nile | *The first child born to a family | A place in Egypt | A kind of plague
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means the eldest child. «The firstborn son sat at the front of the family.» | front | family | *firstborn | sat
test: Which word fits the gap? «Her ___ child was born on a cold morning in January.» | Twin | Adopted | *Firstborn | Youngest
test: What does firstborn mean? | A child who lives far away | *The first child born to a family | A child born in a hospital | The last child born to a family
exam: Ellie says firstborn means a very clever child. Why is she wrong? | Firstborn means very clever in a family | *Firstborn means the first child born to a family, and first and born are the clues | Firstborn means the child who is tallest | Firstborn is a plague in the Bible
